1
00:00:01,167 --> 00:00:02,376
"Previously on The Mentalist..."

2
00:00:02,502 --> 00:00:05,129
- I'm Patrick.
- Hey, Patrick. Lorelei.

3
00:00:05,630 --> 00:00:07,089
Perhaps we can see
each other again.

4
00:00:07,256 --> 00:00:09,342
I do what Red John
tells me to do.

5
00:00:09,926 --> 00:00:12,220
- Accept his friendship.
- It's that easy?

6
00:00:12,345 --> 00:00:14,222
Sure. And you'll need
to bring him a gift.

7
00:00:14,347 --> 00:00:16,682
- What kinda gift?
- Teresa Lisbon's dead body

8
00:00:16,807 --> 00:00:18,226
would be the perfect thing.

9
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:20,770
Good luck, Teresa. Love you.

10
00:00:22,104 --> 00:00:24,398
Well, the question remains,
why did Jane do this?

11
00:00:24,524 --> 00:00:26,359
- Orders from Red John?
- I don't know what to think.

12
00:00:26,484 --> 00:00:28,528
I want arrest warrants prepped
for every single member

13
00:00:28,653 --> 00:00:30,404
of that CBI team, dead or alive.

14
00:00:30,530 --> 00:00:32,073
FBI! Nobody move!

15
00:00:32,198 --> 00:00:33,991
CBI! Don't shoot!
We're CBI agents!

16
00:00:34,116 --> 00:00:35,952
- You're making a terrible mistake.
- Get out.

17
00:00:36,118 --> 00:00:37,745
- Got the gift?
- Red John in there?

18
00:00:38,454 --> 00:00:41,374
Our fake deaths were a ruse
to trap Red John, and it worked.

19
00:00:41,499 --> 00:00:44,544
"What if you and I were friends?
Imagine the life we could lead."

20
00:00:44,710 --> 00:00:45,753
Go to hell.

21
00:00:55,513 --> 00:00:56,806
You're gonna break down
and you're gonna tell us

22
00:00:57,014 --> 00:00:58,349
everything you know
about Red John.

23
00:00:58,474 --> 00:01:00,184
You're gonna sing like a bird.

24
00:01:00,309 --> 00:01:02,311
No, lover. I won't.

25
00:01:02,603 --> 00:01:03,896
Yes, you will.

26
00:01:04,981 --> 00:01:06,148
Yes, you will.

27
00:01:40,891 --> 00:01:43,060
- We're up.
- What?

28
00:01:43,227 --> 00:01:44,520
We have a case.

29
00:01:45,104 --> 00:01:46,230
Now?

30
00:01:46,939 --> 00:01:49,066
You can't talk to her yet anyhow.

31
00:01:49,233 --> 00:01:51,027
The FBI won't let you.

32
00:01:51,152 --> 00:01:52,612
I'll be right there.

33
00:02:16,886 --> 00:02:18,262
You can't leave
your car there.

34
00:02:19,805 --> 00:02:20,931
Hey!

35
00:02:30,149 --> 00:02:31,359
Hey, boys.

36
00:02:32,902 --> 00:02:35,029
- You the responding officer?
- Uh, yes, ma'am.

37
00:02:35,154 --> 00:02:36,697
- Officer Yannick.
- What have we got?

38
00:02:36,906 --> 00:02:40,326
A 911 call came in from this location.
7:33 p.m.

39
00:02:40,451 --> 00:02:42,078
But, uh, nobody spoke.

40
00:02:42,328 --> 00:02:45,623
Door was unlocked, and, uh,
this is how we found 'em.

41
00:02:45,956 --> 00:02:49,168
This is Rex Lango
and, uh, Callie Karlsen.

42
00:02:49,293 --> 00:02:52,505
They both worked together
at the hotel convention center.

43
00:02:52,672 --> 00:02:53,756
Uh, this is her place.

44
00:02:54,215 --> 00:02:56,550
- So the door was already open?
- Yes, sir.

45
00:02:56,926 --> 00:02:59,929
I figure the marks and bruising
on the neck indicate strangulation

46
00:03:00,054 --> 00:03:02,890
and, uh, he got clubbed to death
with the bottle, ah?

47
00:03:03,057 --> 00:03:05,768
Yes. Nice analysis there, Yannick.

48
00:03:06,435 --> 00:03:07,937
Couldn't have killed each other,
could they?

49
00:03:08,062 --> 00:03:09,897
Unlikely. She'd have to be
conscious and active

50
00:03:10,022 --> 00:03:11,357
to hit him with that bottle.

51
00:03:11,482 --> 00:03:13,275
Check out the lipstick
on his cheek.

52
00:03:13,609 --> 00:03:15,236
So it's your classic love triangle.

53
00:03:15,361 --> 00:03:17,488
Third wheel comes in,
finds these two kissing

54
00:03:17,613 --> 00:03:20,282
whacks the rival with the bubbly
chokes out jezebel here.

55
00:03:20,408 --> 00:03:21,826
Yeah, that's pretty much what I...

56
00:03:22,201 --> 00:03:24,370
uh, figured. Yeah.

57
00:03:24,578 --> 00:03:25,871
Jane? Thoughts?

58
00:03:25,996 --> 00:03:28,040
Well, the champagne's
an excellent vintage.

59
00:03:28,165 --> 00:03:30,042
Callie didn't have
a steady boyfriend.

60
00:03:30,209 --> 00:03:31,961
Uh, no spare toothbrush.

61
00:03:32,086 --> 00:03:35,423
She believes poor soul
in a benevolent universe

62
00:03:35,548 --> 00:03:38,509
and she, uh, comes from money.

63
00:03:40,553 --> 00:03:43,764
- Money? She works in a hotel.
- I've seen enough.

64
00:03:43,889 --> 00:03:46,267
We're outta here.
Let forensics do their job.

65
00:03:48,602 --> 00:03:50,646
So, uh, if you need me,
you know where to find me.

66
00:03:50,771 --> 00:03:52,940
- Thank you, officer Yannick.
- You're welcome. My pleasure.

67
00:03:59,405 --> 00:04:00,948
What are you guys doing here?

68
00:04:01,991 --> 00:04:03,409
What are you doing here?

69
00:04:04,243 --> 00:04:05,453
Hey, Teresa.

70
00:04:06,537 --> 00:04:08,539
What's up? You're all under
suspension, aren't you?

71
00:04:08,664 --> 00:04:09,915
We were told to cover your calls.

72
00:04:10,040 --> 00:04:12,001
Suspension? What?
Who are you guys?

73
00:04:12,126 --> 00:04:13,419
FBI. Walk away.

74
00:04:14,336 --> 00:04:16,797
You didn't hear?
The suspensions have been lifted.

75
00:04:16,922 --> 00:04:18,174
The brass made a deal.

76
00:04:18,299 --> 00:04:20,050
Yeah, we heard
that they were talking.

77
00:04:20,176 --> 00:04:21,427
They put a lid
on the whole thing.

78
00:04:21,594 --> 00:04:23,763
It's business as usual.
Suspension's lifted.

79
00:04:23,888 --> 00:04:25,723
So you guys don't need
to be here.

80
00:04:25,848 --> 00:04:27,183
Look, I'm sorry for the mix-up.

81
00:04:27,308 --> 00:04:28,809
Wait. Wait.
You mean to tell me

82
00:04:28,934 --> 00:04:31,228
that after the monumental
crap storm you guys created

83
00:04:31,395 --> 00:04:33,481
they're just gonna let you walk away?

84
00:04:33,856 --> 00:04:35,858
- I'm stunned, frankly.
- I understand.

85
00:04:35,983 --> 00:04:39,195
I mean, you destroyed the career
of a fine FBI agent.

86
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:41,530
You... you caused the death
of your own boss.

87
00:04:41,655 --> 00:04:42,698
And this one?

88
00:04:42,823 --> 00:04:44,241
This one's got assault, narcotics

89
00:04:44,366 --> 00:04:46,118
- and fraud charges against him.
- All dismissed.

90
00:04:46,243 --> 00:04:47,620
Part of the deal. Phew.

91
00:04:48,078 --> 00:04:49,622
How'd you get
such a sweet deal?

92
00:04:49,789 --> 00:04:52,625
Uh, we got a deal because, uh,
it was the FBI that messed up

93
00:04:52,750 --> 00:04:54,877
not me or the CBI.
The FBI.

94
00:04:55,002 --> 00:04:56,629
- That's right.
- That's incorrect.

95
00:04:56,796 --> 00:04:58,214
- Oh, touché.
- We were this close

96
00:04:58,339 --> 00:05:00,257
to catching Red John
before you blew it.

97
00:05:00,382 --> 00:05:02,259
And even in spite of your interference
we caught Lorelei Martins

98
00:05:02,384 --> 00:05:03,719
- and she's our...
- She's our suspect

99
00:05:03,844 --> 00:05:06,013
- and we want her back.
- You're not getting her.

100
00:05:07,139 --> 00:05:08,516
Oh, we'll see about that.

101
00:05:09,266 --> 00:05:10,392
We'll see.

102
00:05:10,518 --> 00:05:11,560
"We'll see"?

103
00:05:11,685 --> 00:05:14,480
Your inarticulate rage is understandable
but it's misplaced.

104
00:05:14,605 --> 00:05:16,607
You should probably just calm down.

105
00:05:16,774 --> 00:05:18,567
You calm yourself down.
I'm not angry.

106
00:05:18,692 --> 00:05:20,319
No? Your temples are pulsing

107
00:05:20,444 --> 00:05:22,321
like some weird
undersea creature.

108
00:05:22,446 --> 00:05:24,532
If that's not anger,
you should see a doctor.

109
00:05:24,657 --> 00:05:26,951
- Jane, stop.
- Okay, I'm going.

110
00:05:27,076 --> 00:05:28,744
Nice to see you.
Watch this one.

111
00:05:28,869 --> 00:05:30,120
He's a hothead.

112
00:05:30,538 --> 00:05:31,831
I am sorry.
He does that.

113
00:05:31,956 --> 00:05:33,582
- I'm not angry.
- I believe you.

114
00:05:33,707 --> 00:05:34,959
I just think you people
should be in jail

115
00:05:35,084 --> 00:05:36,919
- and not out working cases.
- That's right.

116
00:05:37,044 --> 00:05:39,255
But we're not in jail.
We're here, so keep moving.

117
00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:41,257
Or else what,
you're gonna make us move?

118
00:05:42,299 --> 00:05:43,384
If you like.

119
00:05:44,301 --> 00:05:46,053
Then go ahead.
Make me move.

120
00:05:46,178 --> 00:05:48,013
All right, that's enough.
You're both being childish.

121
00:05:48,180 --> 00:05:49,431
- You take your hands off!
- Get off her!

122
00:05:49,557 --> 00:05:51,100
- Whoa. Whoa. Whoa. Whoa.
- Come on.

123
00:05:51,225 --> 00:05:53,018
- Hey!
- Come on!

124
00:05:53,185 --> 00:05:54,270
Break it up!

125
00:05:54,645 --> 00:05:55,855
- Come on.
- Let it go.

126
00:05:55,980 --> 00:05:57,439
- I'm sorry.
- That's it!

127
00:06:00,276 --> 00:06:01,986
I'll see you back at the office.

128
00:06:02,111 --> 00:06:03,445
Knock it off!

129
00:06:03,571 --> 00:06:05,030
Come on, guys!

130
00:06:23,572 --> 00:06:25,532
- Welcome back.
- Thank you so much.

131
00:06:25,657 --> 00:06:27,910
I could not be less happy
to be back.

132
00:06:28,619 --> 00:06:29,870
Uh...

133
00:06:30,621 --> 00:06:33,582
I'd like to take this opportunity
to thank you for, uh...

134
00:06:34,124 --> 00:06:36,376
- fixing things.
- Yes, sir. We...

135
00:06:36,502 --> 00:06:39,421
You know, I thought
I had, as you say

136
00:06:39,546 --> 00:06:40,631
fixed things

137
00:06:40,756 --> 00:06:44,009
{\an8}and now I discover that you
and your FBI counterparts

138
00:06:44,134 --> 00:06:45,803
have been fighting?

139
00:06:45,928 --> 00:06:47,805
{\an8}- At a crime scene?
- Sir, it was...

140
00:06:47,930 --> 00:06:51,725
{\an8}If I can persuade the FBI
to forget this latest incident

141
00:06:51,850 --> 00:06:55,062
{\an8}you, Jane, are down
to your very last chance.

142
00:06:55,312 --> 00:06:56,814
And you are only granted
this chance

143
00:06:56,939 --> 00:06:58,482
{\an8}because to get rid of you now
would be evidence

144
00:06:58,607 --> 00:07:01,026
{\an8}of the scandal we are trying
so hard to conceal!

145
00:07:02,402 --> 00:07:04,029
{\an8}Looking on the bright side

146
00:07:04,154 --> 00:07:05,823
{\an8}we have Lorelei Martins.

147
00:07:05,948 --> 00:07:07,741
She can lead us to Red John.

148
00:07:07,866 --> 00:07:09,201
She knows who he is.

149
00:07:09,701 --> 00:07:12,621
{\an8}California's most notorious
serial killer caught on your watch.

150
00:07:12,746 --> 00:07:14,456
{\an8}Well, that remains
to be seen.

151
00:07:14,581 --> 00:07:16,875
{\an8}But until I negotiate
an arrangement with the feds

152
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:19,670
{\an8}you cannot talk to her.
That's the deal!

153
00:07:19,795 --> 00:07:22,589
{\an8}I understand. But here's the thing.
The FBI can't have her.

154
00:07:22,714 --> 00:07:25,259
{\an8}In a half an hour, I have to stand up
at a press conference

155
00:07:25,384 --> 00:07:28,637
{\an8}and lie to the people of California
in order to protect you.

156
00:07:28,762 --> 00:07:30,472
{\an8}And you are arguing
with me now?

157
00:07:30,597 --> 00:07:31,765
They can't have her.

158
00:07:31,890 --> 00:07:33,392
{\an8}I will do my best
to keep her, but you have...

159
00:07:33,517 --> 00:07:35,727
{\an8}I promise, uh, there'll be
no more trouble from me.

160
00:07:35,853 --> 00:07:37,563
I-I won't say a word
at this press conference.

161
00:07:37,688 --> 00:07:38,939
{\an8}You're damn right you won't
say a word

162
00:07:39,064 --> 00:07:40,649
{\an8}'cause you won't be there!

163
00:07:45,487 --> 00:07:46,905
{\an8}"Agent Schultz!"

164
00:07:47,489 --> 00:07:48,824
{\an8}Alexa.

165
00:07:49,366 --> 00:07:50,409
Hi.

166
00:07:51,034 --> 00:07:52,786
{\an8}We still have a deal, right?

167
00:07:52,911 --> 00:07:55,455
{\an8}I'd rather eat spiders,
but, yeah, we still have a deal.

168
00:07:55,581 --> 00:07:56,832
{\an8}Good, good.

169
00:07:57,040 --> 00:07:58,792
{\an8}God, you look fabulous,
by the way.

170
00:07:58,917 --> 00:08:02,004
{\an8}Camera ready.
Is... is my tie straight?

171
00:08:02,170 --> 00:08:04,631
{\an8}You understand, Gale,
this matter doesn't end here.

172
00:08:04,840 --> 00:08:07,050
{\an8}You have to give us
Lorelei Martins

173
00:08:07,175 --> 00:08:09,136
{\an8}or there'll be consequences
down the line.

174
00:08:09,720 --> 00:08:11,555
Consequences for whom?

175
00:08:11,847 --> 00:08:14,516
{\an8}It was your agents that killed
the best chance we've had yet

176
00:08:14,641 --> 00:08:15,684
{\an8}of catching Red John.

177
00:08:15,809 --> 00:08:17,436
{\an8}It was your Agent Darcy
that killed Wainright.

178
00:08:17,561 --> 00:08:20,355
{\an8}Tragic outcome
in a deadly force situation.

179
00:08:20,647 --> 00:08:22,441
{\an8}Agent Darcy is devastated.

180
00:08:22,566 --> 00:08:24,318
{\an8}She's had a nervous collapse,
in fact.

181
00:08:24,443 --> 00:08:27,070
{\an8}Your people committed
deliberate crimes.

182
00:08:27,195 --> 00:08:28,906
{\an8}Well, that's debatable.

183
00:08:29,031 --> 00:08:30,198
{\an8}Look!

184
00:08:30,324 --> 00:08:32,951
{\an8}We have agreed to a cover-up.
That's the deal.

185
00:08:33,285 --> 00:08:34,661
{\an8}If you're saying now that...

186
00:08:34,786 --> 00:08:37,164
{\an8}you're gonna dig this all up again
unless I do your bidding

187
00:08:37,289 --> 00:08:38,916
{\an8}then no deal.

188
00:08:39,207 --> 00:08:41,627
{\an8}No, let... let's tell
the truth right now.

189
00:08:41,835 --> 00:08:44,212
{\an8}An FBI agent shot and killed
a CBI agent

190
00:08:44,338 --> 00:08:46,006
in the midst of a botched operation.

191
00:08:46,131 --> 00:08:48,592
{\an8}It'll be a huge scandal,
we'll probably lose our jobs

192
00:08:48,717 --> 00:08:51,094
but I'm sure we'll both feel
better for it.

193
00:08:52,012 --> 00:08:53,430
Son of a bitch.

194
00:08:54,765 --> 00:08:56,850
{\an8}I am very proud to tell you
that last week

195
00:08:56,975 --> 00:09:01,563
{\an8}in a joint FBI-CBI sting operation
of great complexity and danger

196
00:09:01,730 --> 00:09:03,774
{\an8}Lorelei Martins,
a close associate

197
00:09:03,899 --> 00:09:07,319
{\an8}of notorious serial killer
Red John, was arrested.

198
00:09:07,611 --> 00:09:09,738
Tragically, in the course
of that operation

199
00:09:09,947 --> 00:09:14,326
CBI Special Agent in charge
Luther Wainright was shot and killed.

200
00:09:14,451 --> 00:09:15,619
Gale?

201
00:09:16,078 --> 00:09:18,830
Luther Wainright was a good friend

202
00:09:18,956 --> 00:09:23,168
a valued colleague, and we all mourn
his passing deeply.

203
00:09:23,543 --> 00:09:24,795
He's a hero.

204
00:09:25,837 --> 00:09:29,049
As part of the sting operation
one of our operatives, Patrick Jane

205
00:09:29,174 --> 00:09:31,551
had criminal charges
fabricated against him

206
00:09:31,677 --> 00:09:33,470
in order to go undercover

207
00:09:33,595 --> 00:09:36,306
and we apologize to the public
for that deception.

208
00:09:36,848 --> 00:09:38,392
Today, the story
is of the great job done

209
00:09:38,517 --> 00:09:41,395
by these two teams
of consummate professionals

210
00:09:41,561 --> 00:09:43,271
working together in harmony.

211
00:09:43,397 --> 00:09:44,648
Questions?

212
00:09:44,815 --> 00:09:48,151
This working in harmony business
is very hard to believe.

213
00:09:48,360 --> 00:09:51,154
There's a very long public
history of disharmony

214
00:09:51,279 --> 00:09:52,364
between your two bureaus.

215
00:09:52,489 --> 00:09:54,324
That's why they call it history, Josh.

216
00:09:54,449 --> 00:09:56,118
- It's in the past.
- Exactly.

217
00:09:56,410 --> 00:09:59,121
What we're celebrating today
is the dawn of a new era.

218
00:09:59,287 --> 00:10:00,539
Just this morning,
these two teams

219
00:10:00,664 --> 00:10:02,416
began work on another
case together.

220
00:10:02,582 --> 00:10:04,876
A double murder
in Dupont Gardens.

221
00:10:05,002 --> 00:10:07,254
Best of luck on that one, guys.
Go get 'em.

222
00:10:15,804 --> 00:10:17,806
Let's call it a truce, shall we, guys?

223
00:10:17,931 --> 00:10:19,307
I mean, we're all grownups here.

224
00:10:19,725 --> 00:10:21,852
- Yep, sure.
- Yeah.

225
00:10:22,686 --> 00:10:24,855
- Nice place.
- It is.

226
00:10:32,029 --> 00:10:35,532
This is like a bad date. I wish
these bozos would just vanish.

227
00:10:38,660 --> 00:10:40,579
Wow. Four cops.

228
00:10:40,954 --> 00:10:42,622
Must be a red ball, huh?

229
00:10:43,206 --> 00:10:44,332
A red ball?

230
00:10:44,458 --> 00:10:46,334
Well, that's what you guys call
an urgent case, right?

231
00:10:46,460 --> 00:10:48,670
All murder cases are urgent.

232
00:10:48,795 --> 00:10:51,673
Yes, of course. I...
I would never imply otherwise. I...

233
00:10:51,798 --> 00:10:53,633
What can you tell us
about Callie and Rex?

234
00:10:53,759 --> 00:10:57,054
Um, Callie has been with us
two years as a housekeeper.

235
00:10:57,179 --> 00:10:59,056
Reliable. Always upbeat.

236
00:10:59,347 --> 00:11:03,560
Really, uh, just a lovely girl.
Well, a woman, that is.

237
00:11:03,685 --> 00:11:06,271
Uh, Rex Lango
I don't know so well.

238
00:11:06,396 --> 00:11:07,773
He's only been here
a couple weeks

239
00:11:07,898 --> 00:11:10,233
and, uh, works over
in tech support.

240
00:11:10,358 --> 00:11:11,943
But he seems like, you know,
a good fellow.

241
00:11:12,069 --> 00:11:13,195
He... uh, punctual.

242
00:11:13,320 --> 00:11:15,363
Were they friends? Lovers?

243
00:11:15,822 --> 00:11:17,574
Uh, well, I wouldn't know.

244
00:11:17,699 --> 00:11:20,702
Um, you know, you should check
with their workmates.

245
00:11:20,827 --> 00:11:22,120
You and Callie were close?

246
00:11:22,245 --> 00:11:23,955
Yes, me and Callie
were friends.

247
00:11:24,081 --> 00:11:26,416
She was such a good,
kind person.

248
00:11:26,792 --> 00:11:28,168
Poor thing.
Oh, my God.

249
00:11:28,293 --> 00:11:30,128
Did she have any boyfriend troubles
that you know of?

250
00:11:30,253 --> 00:11:31,922
Nuh-unh. Men were always
asking her out

251
00:11:32,047 --> 00:11:33,090
but she would always
say no.

252
00:11:33,215 --> 00:11:34,800
Was anybody bothering her?

253
00:11:34,925 --> 00:11:36,134
Not that she told me.

254
00:11:36,259 --> 00:11:38,220
What was her relationship
with Rex Lango?

255
00:11:38,345 --> 00:11:40,555
- None, I don't think.
- Hmm.

256
00:11:41,598 --> 00:11:44,601
What about Mr. Norris?
Did he have a thing for Callie?

257
00:11:44,726 --> 00:11:46,311
Oh, you think Mr. Norris?

258
00:11:49,314 --> 00:11:51,817
He would ogle her.
But he did that to all the women...

259
00:11:51,942 --> 00:11:56,154
ogle them and, you know,
cop a feel sometimes.

260
00:11:56,571 --> 00:11:59,282
He always asks people out,
but nobody says yes

261
00:11:59,407 --> 00:12:01,535
because he had a girlfriend
once who worked here

262
00:12:01,660 --> 00:12:04,162
and they broke up,
and he fired her butt so fast.

263
00:12:04,287 --> 00:12:06,456
- Hmm.
- You think he did this?

264
00:12:10,752 --> 00:12:13,296
- Did you get anything useful?
- Nope. You?

265
00:12:13,421 --> 00:12:14,506
Nope.

266
00:12:14,756 --> 00:12:16,007
Be right back.

267
00:12:16,633 --> 00:12:18,260
Nah, nothing useful.

268
00:12:18,677 --> 00:12:20,804
Uh, excuse me.
Mr. Norris?

269
00:12:21,054 --> 00:12:23,473
Uh, thank you so much
for your help in the investigation.

270
00:12:23,598 --> 00:12:25,684
I just have a couple more questions
before we go.

271
00:12:25,809 --> 00:12:27,936
- Yeah.
- Um... how many employees

272
00:12:28,061 --> 00:12:30,355
are you responsible for
here at the hotel?

273
00:12:30,480 --> 00:12:32,566
I supervise 210 employees.

274
00:12:32,691 --> 00:12:34,025
Wow. That is a lot.

275
00:12:34,151 --> 00:12:35,569
Yeah. Have you ever seen
your mother naked?

276
00:12:35,694 --> 00:12:37,529
What? No!

277
00:12:37,654 --> 00:12:39,072
Well, we'll leave that alone
for a moment.

278
00:12:39,197 --> 00:12:40,365
Let me ask you this.

279
00:12:40,490 --> 00:12:43,910
Have you ever looked
at Callie Karlsen in a sexual way?

280
00:12:44,035 --> 00:12:45,495
No!

281
00:12:45,745 --> 00:12:48,039
I mean, you know,
she's an attractive...

282
00:12:48,373 --> 00:12:49,583
- woman.
- Sure.

283
00:12:50,667 --> 00:12:52,043
I didn't look away.

284
00:12:52,586 --> 00:12:54,921
So, yes, you looked
at her sexually.

285
00:12:55,088 --> 00:12:57,215
- Uh, have you touched her?
- No!

286
00:12:58,592 --> 00:13:01,720
Why are you shielding your right side?
Are you hiding something?

287
00:13:01,845 --> 00:13:03,346
Hiding?
I'm not hiding anything!

288
00:13:03,471 --> 00:13:05,640
Something. Your... your inside
jacket pocket

289
00:13:05,765 --> 00:13:07,142
- is making you nervous.
- No!

290
00:13:07,267 --> 00:13:09,686
- What do you have in there?
- Uh, w... nothing. Oh. Okay.

291
00:13:09,853 --> 00:13:10,937
A wallet.

292
00:13:11,104 --> 00:13:13,273
Wh-why are you wanting
to hide your wallet from us?

293
00:13:13,398 --> 00:13:15,525
I don't. It's just a wallet.

294
00:13:15,817 --> 00:13:17,944
- Hey, you can't do that.
- It's a gray area.

295
00:13:18,069 --> 00:13:19,404
Okay... there's nothing
in there.

296
00:13:19,738 --> 00:13:23,783
Well, looky here. Callie Karlsen.
That's our girl, isn't it?

297
00:13:23,909 --> 00:13:25,660
Couldn't resist a souvenir, huh?

298
00:13:25,785 --> 00:13:28,455
Okay. I have never seen
that before in my life.

299
00:13:29,039 --> 00:13:31,499
Really? Has this wallet been
out of your possession recently?

300
00:13:32,125 --> 00:13:34,419
No, but... I swear,
I-I've never seen that before.

301
00:13:34,544 --> 00:13:37,005
- I swear to God.
- Well, I tell you what, Mr. Norris.

302
00:13:37,130 --> 00:13:38,632
Why don't we talk some
more downtown

303
00:13:38,757 --> 00:13:39,841
see if we can solve
this mystery?

304
00:13:39,966 --> 00:13:41,968
No. No, no, no. No, no.
I've got a hotel to run.

305
00:13:42,135 --> 00:13:43,887
- I cannot...
- Whoa, whoa, whoa! Wait a second.

306
00:13:44,012 --> 00:13:45,305
He's our suspect.

307
00:13:45,430 --> 00:13:47,849
- Looks like he's ours to me.
- No, no. That's not fair.

308
00:13:47,974 --> 00:13:50,977
Fair? What are you,
seven years old? Fair!

309
00:13:51,269 --> 00:13:53,063
Tell you what.
You give us Lorelei Martins

310
00:13:53,188 --> 00:13:54,648
we'll give you this guy.

311
00:13:55,857 --> 00:13:58,902
That's fair.
No? Okay. Bye-bye.

312
00:14:01,988 --> 00:14:03,406
Bastards.

313
00:14:03,531 --> 00:14:06,576
Hey, no need to be so grumpy.
You got your wish.

314
00:14:06,910 --> 00:14:08,620
You wanted them to vanish?

315
00:14:08,828 --> 00:14:10,121
Vanished.

316
00:14:10,956 --> 00:14:13,375
What is so funny?
They took our suspect.

317
00:14:13,500 --> 00:14:15,961
- No, they took their suspect.
- Norris isn't our man?

318
00:14:16,086 --> 00:14:18,338
Small hands, addicted to routine.

319
00:14:18,463 --> 00:14:20,966
No way a man like that
strangles a woman on impulse.

320
00:14:21,091 --> 00:14:22,592
- But the photos in his wallet
- Planted.

321
00:14:22,717 --> 00:14:23,885
I took them
from Callie's apartment

322
00:14:24,010 --> 00:14:25,428
for just such an occasion.

323
00:14:25,553 --> 00:14:28,515
You know full well that is illegal
in 20 different ways.

324
00:14:28,974 --> 00:14:31,685
- What about your promise to Bertram?
- I had my fingers crossed.

325
00:14:31,810 --> 00:14:34,646
Didn't you wish for Mancini and Smith
to just disappear?

326
00:14:34,771 --> 00:14:37,857
Well, voila, your wish
was granted, like magic.

327
00:14:37,983 --> 00:14:39,818
Now we can focus
on catching the real killer

328
00:14:39,943 --> 00:14:41,653
while the FBI's dealing
with Norris.

329
00:14:41,778 --> 00:14:43,280
That is not the point.

330
00:14:46,616 --> 00:14:49,786
"We're supposed to be rebuilding
our relationship with the FBI."

331
00:14:49,911 --> 00:14:52,330
- Rebuilding trust.
- Trust is not an option.

332
00:14:52,455 --> 00:14:54,499
Red John has a friend
inside the FBI.

333
00:14:54,666 --> 00:14:57,961
If they get hold of Lorelei,
she will die or escape.

334
00:14:58,128 --> 00:15:00,255
Oh, God, here we go.
How do you know that?

335
00:15:00,380 --> 00:15:02,090
Red John told me.

336
00:15:02,215 --> 00:15:04,926
Well, he was lying, of course,
to muddy the waters.

337
00:15:05,260 --> 00:15:06,761
Why would he tell you
the truth?

338
00:15:06,886 --> 00:15:09,931
Because he knows we'll assume
he's lying.

339
00:15:10,682 --> 00:15:13,977
And he knows we'll begin to suspect
the truth anyway.

340
00:15:14,102 --> 00:15:17,314
It's a double bluff
to conceal his friend.

341
00:15:17,772 --> 00:15:20,275
Or he's lying
and he has no friend in the FBI.

342
00:15:20,400 --> 00:15:21,735
Why are you so determined
to believe that?

343
00:15:21,860 --> 00:15:24,321
Because I would like to feel
solid ground under my feet.

344
00:15:24,446 --> 00:15:26,489
I would like to trust somebody
or something.

345
00:15:26,614 --> 00:15:28,908
You know, you, with your wheels
within wheels...

346
00:15:29,034 --> 00:15:31,161
you're driving me nuts.

347
00:15:38,633 --> 00:15:40,384
- Hey, boss.
- Hey, Grace.

348
00:15:41,552 --> 00:15:43,137
Where are we
with Karlsen and Lango?

349
00:15:43,262 --> 00:15:44,639
Uh, looked into the phone records.

350
00:15:44,764 --> 00:15:46,766
No calls in or out
for Lango that evening.

351
00:15:46,891 --> 00:15:49,810
Callie Karlsen called
Nicola Karlsen at 7:15

352
00:15:49,935 --> 00:15:51,687
18 minutes
before the 911 call.

353
00:15:51,812 --> 00:15:54,190
Hey, boss. Where's the FBI?

354
00:15:54,315 --> 00:15:56,317
They are pursuing other inquiries.

355
00:15:56,484 --> 00:15:58,861
- Sweet!
- Listen to me.

356
00:15:58,986 --> 00:16:02,573
The FBI is a fine organization
and they are our partners.

357
00:16:02,698 --> 00:16:05,493
We need to work with them.
They deserve our respect and our trust.

358
00:16:05,618 --> 00:16:07,578
- Am I clear?
- Yeah.

359
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:14,794
- Did you contact the sister?
- Yes.

360
00:16:14,919 --> 00:16:17,004
She lives out in Boone.
She was out of contact

361
00:16:17,129 --> 00:16:19,924
for two days at a swap meet in Tahoe.
Got home this morning.

362
00:16:20,049 --> 00:16:22,385
- The local sheriff gave her the news.
- What's her story?

363
00:16:22,510 --> 00:16:26,055
Oh, the Karlsen family used to own
half of Alameda county.

364
00:16:26,180 --> 00:16:27,932
Lost it all in the crash of '06

365
00:16:28,057 --> 00:16:30,559
parents died a year later...
highway collision.

366
00:16:31,060 --> 00:16:34,480
Nicola is the older sister.
Single mom, two kids.

367
00:16:34,772 --> 00:16:36,899
Jewelry designer is what
it says on her I.R.S. forms.

368
00:16:37,024 --> 00:16:38,067
What about Lango?

369
00:16:38,192 --> 00:16:39,694
Moved to town from L.A.
six months ago.

370
00:16:39,819 --> 00:16:42,029
No rap sheet on him.
No relatives or friends nearby.

371
00:16:42,196 --> 00:16:43,656
We went through his apartment.
Nothing.

372
00:16:43,781 --> 00:16:45,241
Bare bones.
Mattress on the floor.

373
00:16:45,366 --> 00:16:46,617
Running from something, maybe?

374
00:16:46,742 --> 00:16:48,869
Keep digging on Lango.
It sounds promising.

375
00:16:48,994 --> 00:16:50,871
Jane and I will go
talk to the sister.

376
00:16:50,996 --> 00:16:52,581
You two go and canvass
the crime scene

377
00:16:52,707 --> 00:16:55,251
like you should have instead
of fighting with the FBI!

378
00:16:56,419 --> 00:16:57,753
- Yes, boss.
- Yes, boss.

379
00:17:09,432 --> 00:17:10,516
Hey, Yannick.

380
00:17:10,933 --> 00:17:12,017
Agents.

381
00:17:12,226 --> 00:17:14,395
- Thanks for your help.
- No problemo.

382
00:17:14,562 --> 00:17:16,397
Just don't hit me, okay?

383
00:17:16,647 --> 00:17:18,023
Funny.

384
00:17:18,315 --> 00:17:21,235
Hey, no offense, but...
I never saw that before.

385
00:17:21,360 --> 00:17:23,779
Law enforcement agents
fighting it out in the street?

386
00:17:23,904 --> 00:17:25,865
You guys are hard-core, man!

387
00:17:30,035 --> 00:17:32,705
Yes. Uh, so, anyway,
we started canvassing already.

388
00:17:33,205 --> 00:17:34,665
Nothing useful so far.

389
00:17:34,790 --> 00:17:36,250
- Let's check out the rest of...
- Yeah.

390
00:17:43,424 --> 00:17:45,551
All right. Thank you very much
for your time. Appreciate it.

391
00:17:55,603 --> 00:17:57,146
Saw a young fellow
over there...

392
00:17:57,271 --> 00:17:59,231
same one they've been showing
on the TV...

393
00:17:59,398 --> 00:18:00,733
got beat to death.

394
00:18:00,900 --> 00:18:02,443
And you saw just one man?

395
00:18:02,568 --> 00:18:04,278
- Rex Lango?
- Yes, sir.

396
00:18:04,403 --> 00:18:06,489
Knocking on her door
about 6:30.

397
00:18:06,614 --> 00:18:09,074
We were sitting out in the sun,
then we came inside.

398
00:18:09,241 --> 00:18:10,743
Did you ever see him
around here before?

399
00:18:11,035 --> 00:18:12,453
No, first time.

400
00:18:12,661 --> 00:18:14,580
She didn't have visitors much.

401
00:18:15,247 --> 00:18:17,708
And then later we heard
a scream from over that way

402
00:18:17,833 --> 00:18:20,544
just a little short one,
like, uh, "Aah!"

403
00:18:23,255 --> 00:18:25,716
- And you weren't concerned?
- Well, no.

404
00:18:25,841 --> 00:18:29,011
At the time, I thought it was
you know, passion.

405
00:18:29,428 --> 00:18:32,223
I said to Bucky, "Good for her".

406
00:18:32,389 --> 00:18:34,642
"That Karlsen girl
got a boyfriend at last."

407
00:18:34,767 --> 00:18:35,935
And what time was this?

408
00:18:36,060 --> 00:18:37,102
I know what time it was

409
00:18:37,228 --> 00:18:39,146
because we were checking
our lottery tickets on the TV.

410
00:18:39,271 --> 00:18:41,315
It was 10 past 7:00.

411
00:18:41,649 --> 00:18:44,443
Here's me thinking
her luck had changed

412
00:18:44,944 --> 00:18:47,488
when really, she was dying.

413
00:18:49,156 --> 00:18:50,533
Poor girl.

414
00:19:08,300 --> 00:19:10,636
Hello. Nicola Larson?

415
00:19:10,761 --> 00:19:13,597
Hi. Um, you must be the CBI.

416
00:19:14,265 --> 00:19:16,100
We're very sorry
for your loss.

417
00:19:17,726 --> 00:19:20,437
Uh, girls, could you maybe take
the boys to your place

418
00:19:20,604 --> 00:19:22,106
watch some TV or something?

419
00:19:22,231 --> 00:19:24,859
Sure. Come on, guys.
Let's go.

420
00:19:28,404 --> 00:19:31,365
I was at a crafts fair
in the Sierras.

421
00:19:31,824 --> 00:19:33,993
The hippie geniuses in charge
picked a place

422
00:19:34,118 --> 00:19:37,079
with great vibes
and no cell phone reception.

423
00:19:37,246 --> 00:19:39,081
So I didn't get this message.

424
00:19:39,498 --> 00:19:42,585
"Nic!
Call me as soon as you can!"

425
00:19:44,295 --> 00:19:47,006
I didn't get that call till last night
when I came home.

426
00:19:47,214 --> 00:19:49,508
Then I called her,
and called...

427
00:19:50,342 --> 00:19:53,178
and called, and then the sheriff
came by this morning.

428
00:19:55,264 --> 00:19:57,391
Nicola, tell us about your sister.

429
00:19:57,558 --> 00:20:00,769
To be honest, we haven't found
a motive yet.

430
00:20:02,062 --> 00:20:03,814
Who would wanna hurt Callie?

431
00:20:04,773 --> 00:20:06,358
I mean, she was a warm,
happy spirit.

432
00:20:06,483 --> 00:20:07,693
Everybody loved her.

433
00:20:07,818 --> 00:20:10,112
Did she have any failed relationships
in her past?

434
00:20:10,404 --> 00:20:11,447
No.

435
00:20:11,614 --> 00:20:12,907
What about feuds with neighbors

436
00:20:13,032 --> 00:20:15,951
or financial disputes,
maybe somebody who felt burned

437
00:20:16,076 --> 00:20:17,745
when your family's business
went under?

438
00:20:17,870 --> 00:20:19,538
We paid off all the debts.

439
00:20:19,747 --> 00:20:22,416
All of them.
That's why I'm here doing this...

440
00:20:23,709 --> 00:20:26,378
And Callie was cleaning rooms
instead of going to college.

441
00:20:27,463 --> 00:20:29,256
Wow, you make some
beautiful things here.

442
00:20:29,673 --> 00:20:30,966
Thank you.

443
00:20:31,091 --> 00:20:32,593
Do you know Rex Lango?

444
00:20:33,177 --> 00:20:34,720
Is that the man
who died with her?

445
00:20:36,221 --> 00:20:38,098
No, I've never heard
the name before.

446
00:20:38,223 --> 00:20:39,558
Well, it seems that, uh...

447
00:20:39,683 --> 00:20:43,604
Callie and Rex were about to drink
a very nice vintage champagne...

448
00:20:43,729 --> 00:20:47,733
1975. About, uh, 500 bucks
a bottle, I'd guess.

449
00:20:47,858 --> 00:20:49,318
At least.

450
00:20:49,693 --> 00:20:51,904
That was the last
from my dad's cellar.

451
00:20:53,280 --> 00:20:55,157
There's no way Callie'd take it
out of the fridge herself.

452
00:20:55,282 --> 00:20:57,159
She'd been saving that bottle
for years

453
00:20:57,284 --> 00:21:00,412
for a special occasion,
like a talisman.

454
00:21:00,579 --> 00:21:03,916
She would've told you
if there was a relationship brewing

455
00:21:04,041 --> 00:21:05,334
with her and Lango?

456
00:21:05,459 --> 00:21:07,920
Yes. Absolutely.

457
00:21:09,129 --> 00:21:10,589
We're very close.

458
00:21:11,215 --> 00:21:13,342
Callie was not interested
in finding a man.

459
00:21:13,509 --> 00:21:16,387
She wanted to go to college first
and get her career going.

460
00:21:16,512 --> 00:21:18,263
And what kind of career
did she want?

461
00:21:19,974 --> 00:21:21,850
She had all kinds of big hopes.

462
00:21:22,810 --> 00:21:25,312
She was the optimist
of the two of us.

463
00:21:25,646 --> 00:21:28,273
She always said our luck
was gonna turn somehow.

464
00:21:30,067 --> 00:21:31,402
I always said...

465
00:21:32,152 --> 00:21:33,821
"Don't hold your breath."

466
00:21:36,073 --> 00:21:37,408
Oh, sorry.

467
00:21:38,742 --> 00:21:40,244
Excuse me.
I have to take this.

468
00:21:41,996 --> 00:21:43,914
- Hello?
- "There's good news, Jane."

469
00:21:44,039 --> 00:21:46,667
The FBI folded on Lorelei Martins.
She's all yours.

470
00:21:46,792 --> 00:21:49,003
Folded?
Well, that's not like them.

471
00:21:49,128 --> 00:21:50,421
You want her or not?

472
00:21:50,546 --> 00:21:52,297
Yes. I'm on my way.

473
00:22:00,472 --> 00:22:02,182
Uh, we need to go soon.

474
00:22:05,144 --> 00:22:06,812
That's all for now, Nicola.

475
00:22:08,022 --> 00:22:09,481
But I want you to know

476
00:22:09,690 --> 00:22:12,443
we're gonna do everything we can
to bring whoever did this to justice.

477
00:22:12,609 --> 00:22:15,279
- Yes, we sure will.
- I don't really care who did this.

478
00:22:15,487 --> 00:22:17,865
Justice for them
won't help Callie or me.

479
00:22:21,535 --> 00:22:22,828
That was rude.
I'm sorry.

480
00:22:22,953 --> 00:22:24,413
It's your job.
I'm sure you do it very well.

481
00:22:24,538 --> 00:22:27,041
No apology needed.
You make a very valid point.

482
00:22:27,166 --> 00:22:30,711
Can I ask you... how much is this
particular one?

483
00:22:34,506 --> 00:22:36,884
- What are you thinking?
- She's ready to crack.

484
00:22:37,259 --> 00:22:38,510
Nicola?

485
00:22:39,344 --> 00:22:40,512
Lorelei.

486
00:22:40,637 --> 00:22:43,724
I meant, what are you thinking
of the case we're working on now?

487
00:22:43,849 --> 00:22:47,144
Well, that one's a puzzler, isn't it?
What the hell is the motive?

488
00:22:47,352 --> 00:22:49,354
I don't think it was the sister.
I like her.

489
00:22:49,938 --> 00:22:51,857
So did you buy that bracelet
for Lorelei?

490
00:22:51,982 --> 00:22:54,359
No, just a whim.
I liked it.

491
00:22:56,904 --> 00:22:59,406
When I talk to her,
I need to be alone.

492
00:22:59,531 --> 00:23:01,158
You will be.

493
00:23:01,325 --> 00:23:05,412
I mean, with nobody watching
or listening.

494
00:23:06,997 --> 00:23:08,916
I need to be able
to tell her truthfully

495
00:23:09,083 --> 00:23:11,001
that we are alone.

496
00:23:15,964 --> 00:23:17,591
- Okay.
- Thank you.

497
00:23:18,175 --> 00:23:19,760
Just be careful.

498
00:23:19,885 --> 00:23:21,428
Don't get pulled into her game.

499
00:23:22,179 --> 00:23:24,765
- What game is that?
- I don't know. You tell me.

500
00:23:25,099 --> 00:23:27,726
Well, I'm supposed to tell you
a game that you're thinking of?

501
00:23:28,185 --> 00:23:31,396
Okay. Uh, you're thinking
of, uh, Twister?

502
00:23:31,772 --> 00:23:33,190
Go ahead. Laugh.

503
00:23:33,315 --> 00:23:34,858
But she's practically
the first person

504
00:23:35,025 --> 00:23:37,569
since your wife that you've,
you know...

505
00:23:37,986 --> 00:23:39,363
Ohh.

506
00:23:39,530 --> 00:23:42,199
It wouldn't be surprising
if you had feelings for her.

507
00:23:42,449 --> 00:23:45,202
She's a stepping stone
to Red John.

508
00:23:45,327 --> 00:23:48,330
I knew that from the beginning.
I don't have any feelings for her.

509
00:24:05,639 --> 00:24:06,890
Hello, Patrick.

510
00:24:08,016 --> 00:24:09,226
Lorelei.

511
00:24:10,477 --> 00:24:12,729
Is it just us, or are
your friends listening?

512
00:24:13,272 --> 00:24:16,191
- "It's just us. We're alone."
- "Good."

513
00:24:16,692 --> 00:24:18,110
"It's much nicer that way."

514
00:24:23,871 --> 00:24:25,957
Sorry I didn't come
to visit you sooner.

515
00:24:26,082 --> 00:24:27,708
I've been a little busy
with a case.

516
00:24:28,042 --> 00:24:29,460
It's okay.

517
00:24:29,669 --> 00:24:31,671
I've been enjoying
the peace and quiet.

518
00:24:31,796 --> 00:24:33,214
Is there anything you need?

519
00:24:33,923 --> 00:24:35,299
I'm fine.

520
00:24:35,549 --> 00:24:37,677
Never mind about me.
How are you?

521
00:24:38,052 --> 00:24:39,804
"Back to solving crimes, huh?"

522
00:24:40,221 --> 00:24:41,639
Yeah.

523
00:24:44,266 --> 00:24:45,810
Why do you bother?

524
00:24:46,519 --> 00:24:49,271
You're trying to hold back
the tide with a broom.

525
00:24:49,397 --> 00:24:50,940
What good are you doing?

526
00:24:52,692 --> 00:24:53,818
I think...

527
00:24:54,485 --> 00:24:57,321
you do it to be close
to Teresa Lisbon.

528
00:24:58,698 --> 00:25:01,158
"I think you're a little bit
in love with her."

529
00:25:06,330 --> 00:25:08,165
I-I do it to, uh...

530
00:25:09,375 --> 00:25:10,835
pass the time.

531
00:25:12,586 --> 00:25:14,171
What good are you doing?

532
00:25:15,214 --> 00:25:16,716
Not much in here.

533
00:25:16,841 --> 00:25:18,718
But I'll be out soon enough.

534
00:25:18,884 --> 00:25:21,178
How and when is up
to Red John.

535
00:25:21,345 --> 00:25:23,014
You think he'll get you outta this?

536
00:25:24,306 --> 00:25:26,392
He'll kill you.
It's easier.

537
00:25:26,517 --> 00:25:28,728
That's okay,
if that's what he wants.

538
00:25:28,853 --> 00:25:30,604
You're that far under his control?

539
00:25:31,647 --> 00:25:34,400
He'll kill you as well
if that's what he wants.

540
00:25:34,525 --> 00:25:36,027
You just can't accept
the fact.

541
00:25:36,152 --> 00:25:37,737
I can make you a better offer.

542
00:25:37,862 --> 00:25:39,447
No killing.

543
00:25:39,613 --> 00:25:42,700
I can get you outta here now...
today, if you want.

544
00:25:42,825 --> 00:25:45,578
I can get you money,
a new identity

545
00:25:45,703 --> 00:25:49,373
uh, set you up with a new life
far away from here.

546
00:25:49,498 --> 00:25:51,625
- "You can do that?"
- "Yes, I can."

547
00:25:52,793 --> 00:25:55,713
I can do anything you want
if you give me Red John.

548
00:26:02,386 --> 00:26:03,804
I want...

549
00:26:04,680 --> 00:26:06,015
your trust

550
00:26:06,724 --> 00:26:08,350
and friendship.

551
00:26:08,517 --> 00:26:10,853
- You have that.
- I don't believe you.

552
00:26:11,812 --> 00:26:13,481
How can I make you believe?

553
00:26:16,358 --> 00:26:17,610
Kiss me.

554
00:26:19,278 --> 00:26:20,821
What does that prove?

555
00:26:22,823 --> 00:26:25,743
First you say
you'll do anything I want

556
00:26:25,868 --> 00:26:28,204
then you refuse
the first thing I ask for.

557
00:26:28,913 --> 00:26:30,915
You're very complicated.

558
00:26:41,300 --> 00:26:42,927
Let me get you outta here.

559
00:26:46,514 --> 00:26:49,308
- I need time to think.
- Not for long.

560
00:26:50,059 --> 00:26:52,770
I don't know how much longer
we're gonna get to keep you here.

561
00:26:54,230 --> 00:26:56,190
We'll talk again this evening.

562
00:27:06,700 --> 00:27:08,744
What are you? Huh?
Crazy?

563
00:27:08,869 --> 00:27:11,038
- Excuse me?
- I told you to be careful.

564
00:27:11,163 --> 00:27:12,498
I told you not to go over
the edge.

565
00:27:12,623 --> 00:27:13,999
And I told you not to listen.

566
00:27:14,125 --> 00:27:15,918
Don't be childish!
I am not your girlfriend.

567
00:27:16,043 --> 00:27:18,712
I am an officer of the law.
How could I not listen?

568
00:27:20,256 --> 00:27:23,092
You kissed her.
You offered to help her escape.

569
00:27:23,217 --> 00:27:25,302
And I would ask her to marry me
if I thought she'd buy it.

570
00:27:25,427 --> 00:27:28,055
- I was playing her.
- She's playing you.

571
00:27:28,180 --> 00:27:29,682
We should've given her
to the feds.

572
00:27:39,525 --> 00:27:43,320
Um, M.E. sent his report
on Callie and Rex.

573
00:27:43,487 --> 00:27:46,031
Confirmed it's not possible
they killed each other.

574
00:27:46,157 --> 00:27:47,950
And Callie had
a small white feather

575
00:27:48,075 --> 00:27:49,368
lodged in the back
of her mouth.

576
00:27:49,493 --> 00:27:52,037
- A feather, huh? Like from a pillow?
- Right.

577
00:27:52,163 --> 00:27:54,748
Which suggests Callie
was strangled by hand

578
00:27:54,874 --> 00:27:57,626
and suffocated with a pillow,
probably in that order.

579
00:27:58,127 --> 00:28:00,462
Why two methods?
Two different people?

580
00:28:00,588 --> 00:28:01,922
Or the killer wasn't
strong enough

581
00:28:02,047 --> 00:28:03,799
- to complete the strangulation.
- Right.

582
00:28:03,966 --> 00:28:06,218
- A woman?
- Women can strangle people.

583
00:28:06,343 --> 00:28:08,053
Oh, believe me, I know I could.

584
00:28:08,179 --> 00:28:09,263
Where's Cho and Rigsby?

585
00:28:09,430 --> 00:28:12,474
I got a line on Rex Lango finally.
Changed his name.

586
00:28:12,600 --> 00:28:15,060
Used to be Erzat Lonagul
out of Bakersfield.

587
00:28:15,186 --> 00:28:17,688
Cho and Rigsby drove down there
to speak to his family.

588
00:28:26,697 --> 00:28:29,742
Nobody could say his name,
so he changed it to Rex.

589
00:28:30,492 --> 00:28:32,828
He was gonna be
a big businessman

590
00:28:32,953 --> 00:28:35,372
and he thought
that sounded rich.

591
00:28:35,581 --> 00:28:36,916
Rex Lango.

592
00:28:37,041 --> 00:28:39,210
Was there any particular business
he was interested in?

593
00:28:39,335 --> 00:28:41,378
You know, he was good
at computers.

594
00:28:41,503 --> 00:28:43,505
But he didn't know yet exactly.

595
00:28:44,048 --> 00:28:46,800
The Internet, robots

596
00:28:46,926 --> 00:28:48,052
or whatever.

597
00:28:48,219 --> 00:28:50,554
Any brushes with the law?
Shady friends?

598
00:28:50,721 --> 00:28:53,265
No.
My cousin was a good man.

599
00:28:53,682 --> 00:28:54,892
Ah!

600
00:28:55,017 --> 00:28:58,145
He was a good man
and he's gone now, so be nice.

601
00:28:58,270 --> 00:28:59,980
He was a bum!

602
00:29:00,105 --> 00:29:02,483
He was not.
He nearly always had a job

603
00:29:02,608 --> 00:29:04,693
and he was never
in trouble with the law.

604
00:29:04,944 --> 00:29:06,445
Is that a bum?

605
00:29:07,196 --> 00:29:10,324
He was never in trouble
because he was too sneaky!

606
00:29:10,574 --> 00:29:12,910
The kid was stealing candy
and quarters

607
00:29:13,035 --> 00:29:14,578
from before he could walk.

608
00:29:14,745 --> 00:29:17,414
And then he would lie to your face
like a drug seller!

609
00:29:17,539 --> 00:29:19,875
He was a dog
to the women always!

610
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:21,377
A bum!

611
00:29:27,007 --> 00:29:30,094
Scheming, dishonest, greedy,
selfish womanizer.

612
00:29:30,219 --> 00:29:32,096
Yeah, but not a criminal.
Just a creep.

613
00:29:32,221 --> 00:29:34,974
He left Bakersfield two years ago
to avoid a paternity suit.

614
00:29:35,224 --> 00:29:38,269
They had no idea he was in SAC.
Last they heard, he was in L.A.

615
00:29:38,394 --> 00:29:39,937
Hmm. That's interesting.

616
00:29:40,062 --> 00:29:41,814
So like I said,
it's a love triangle.

617
00:29:41,981 --> 00:29:43,565
But we've got no jealous boyfriend

618
00:29:43,691 --> 00:29:46,151
and I can't see Callie
dating a sleaze like him.

619
00:29:46,318 --> 00:29:48,362
And she logged no calls
or texts to him, right?

620
00:29:48,529 --> 00:29:50,864
Nope.
I'm waiting for her e-mail records.

621
00:29:51,073 --> 00:29:52,449
I couldn't get them direct
from her P.C.

622
00:29:52,574 --> 00:29:53,659
The hard drive is fried.

623
00:29:53,784 --> 00:29:57,037
Oh. Well, that's why
he was there.

624
00:29:57,246 --> 00:29:58,580
He was in tech support, right?

625
00:29:58,706 --> 00:30:01,250
So he offers to fix her computer.
How could she refuse?

626
00:30:01,417 --> 00:30:03,377
- And then what happened?
- I don't know.

627
00:30:03,502 --> 00:30:05,838
I gotta run. Lorelei's on her way up
from holding.

628
00:30:08,257 --> 00:30:09,383
Wait.

629
00:30:11,218 --> 00:30:13,220
We still haven't resolved
our issue.

630
00:30:13,345 --> 00:30:15,222
I don't think you should be
talking to Lorelei.

631
00:30:15,347 --> 00:30:16,849
- You're too close.
- Well, I disagree.

632
00:30:16,974 --> 00:30:18,434
I could put a stop to this right now.

633
00:30:18,559 --> 00:30:20,853
- One word to Bertram about what you've...
- Please don't do that.

634
00:30:21,145 --> 00:30:22,813
I know I can turn her.

635
00:30:22,938 --> 00:30:24,440
I know I can.

636
00:30:24,606 --> 00:30:26,817
And I promise you
I will be careful.

637
00:30:32,656 --> 00:30:33,866
Thank you.

638
00:30:41,415 --> 00:30:42,583
- Hello.
- Hey.

639
00:30:42,708 --> 00:30:45,210
Stand down, man.
I'm taking charge of this prisoner.

640
00:30:45,336 --> 00:30:46,545
I'm sorry.
What are you talking about?

641
00:30:46,670 --> 00:30:48,922
This is a federal judge's warrant
transferring custody

642
00:30:49,048 --> 00:30:50,632
- of Lorelei to the FBI.
- No, no, no. You can't do that.

643
00:30:50,758 --> 00:30:51,800
- Back off.
- No, don't touch me.

644
00:30:51,925 --> 00:30:53,635
- Hey, wait. Wha...?
- Let's go.

645
00:30:53,761 --> 00:30:55,471
- I need you to step back, sir.
- Don't let them take me.

646
00:30:55,596 --> 00:30:56,638
- Step back.
- Patrick!

647
00:30:56,764 --> 00:30:58,515
- You can't just take her!
- Patrick!

648
00:30:58,724 --> 00:30:59,808
Back it up.

649
00:30:59,933 --> 00:31:01,518
Patrick!

650
00:31:04,411 --> 00:31:06,705
There isn't a choice.
We have to get her back.

651
00:31:06,830 --> 00:31:08,957
Jane, the FBI outfoxed us.

652
00:31:09,124 --> 00:31:11,751
Th-they only pretended
to give up Lorelei

653
00:31:11,877 --> 00:31:13,795
while they were preparing
the warrant to take her.

654
00:31:13,962 --> 00:31:16,590
We should've known they wouldn't fold.
Just deal with it.

655
00:31:16,715 --> 00:31:19,342
I-I'd have to strong-arm a judge
and the FBI

656
00:31:19,468 --> 00:31:21,136
into an arbitration hearing,
and even then...

657
00:31:21,261 --> 00:31:22,304
Well, do it.

658
00:31:22,429 --> 00:31:24,806
The FBI know
how to interrogate people.

659
00:31:24,931 --> 00:31:26,224
They'll do a fine job.

660
00:31:26,349 --> 00:31:28,226
They will either kill her,
or she'll escape.

661
00:31:28,351 --> 00:31:30,979
And we will lose our best chance...
the best chance we have had

662
00:31:31,104 --> 00:31:32,272
of getting to Red John.

663
00:31:32,397 --> 00:31:34,399
Kill her? Uh, what... why?

664
00:31:34,524 --> 00:31:37,027
The... the FBI?
D-don't be ridiculous.

665
00:31:37,444 --> 00:31:41,239
Red John has a friend
high up in the FBI.

666
00:31:41,364 --> 00:31:43,533
Oh, please.
Now how do you know that?

667
00:31:43,658 --> 00:31:45,702
- He told me.
- Well, there you go.

668
00:31:46,036 --> 00:31:49,164
If we don't get her, I will blow
this whole cover-up wide open.

669
00:31:49,289 --> 00:31:52,083
The truth of Wainright's death,
all over the news.

670
00:31:52,209 --> 00:31:54,669
If you do that,
this whole deal collapses

671
00:31:54,794 --> 00:31:56,630
- and you go to jail.
- I don't care.

672
00:31:57,297 --> 00:32:00,675
You call a hearing, or I will be
very glad to sing like a bird.

673
00:32:12,604 --> 00:32:14,773
Well, I've studied all the documents
in this matter

674
00:32:14,898 --> 00:32:16,691
and it is very clear to me

675
00:32:16,816 --> 00:32:19,152
that all of you people
are lying through your teeth.

676
00:32:19,277 --> 00:32:21,154
- Judge...
- No, I don't wanna know.

677
00:32:21,363 --> 00:32:23,490
Whatever sordid errors

678
00:32:23,615 --> 00:32:26,117
you're all conspiring
to cover up

679
00:32:26,243 --> 00:32:27,536
I don't wanna know.

680
00:32:28,036 --> 00:32:30,705
The sole purpose of this meeting
is to decide

681
00:32:30,830 --> 00:32:34,543
who is best equipped to have custody
of Lorelei Martins.

682
00:32:34,709 --> 00:32:36,753
I will decide in favor
of whichever side

683
00:32:36,878 --> 00:32:39,214
irritates me the least.

684
00:32:39,339 --> 00:32:43,385
I will tolerate no misbehavior
of any kind.

685
00:32:43,760 --> 00:32:45,845
Proceed with care.

686
00:32:45,971 --> 00:32:48,265
Your Honor, I would ask you

687
00:32:48,390 --> 00:32:50,725
to simply to look at the record
of Patrick Jane.

688
00:32:50,850 --> 00:32:52,978
Red John killed his family.

689
00:32:53,186 --> 00:32:55,647
Lorelei Martins is a close confederate
of Red John.

690
00:32:55,814 --> 00:32:57,482
How can this man possibly
treat her

691
00:32:57,607 --> 00:33:00,569
with the clarity
and the objectivity required?

692
00:33:00,694 --> 00:33:02,779
He's not a trained professional.

693
00:33:03,280 --> 00:33:04,698
He's a vigilante.

694
00:33:04,823 --> 00:33:06,700
And that alone
should disqualify the CBI

695
00:33:06,825 --> 00:33:08,618
from custody in this matter.

696
00:33:08,743 --> 00:33:11,746
For many years,
I have been pursuing Red John.

697
00:33:12,330 --> 00:33:15,709
I know this case better
than anybody else.

698
00:33:15,875 --> 00:33:19,588
These people, they don't know
how to make Lorelei Martins talk.

699
00:33:19,963 --> 00:33:22,340
- I do.
- If I may interject

700
00:33:22,507 --> 00:33:24,426
Miss Martins tells us

701
00:33:24,551 --> 00:33:27,762
that she has had sexual
relations with Mr. Jane.

702
00:33:28,305 --> 00:33:30,599
That may be the source
of his confidence.

703
00:33:30,724 --> 00:33:32,225
Is that so?

704
00:33:32,350 --> 00:33:33,810
Yes, it is.

705
00:33:34,144 --> 00:33:37,397
We have a relationship.
Uh, that's a good thing.

706
00:33:37,689 --> 00:33:39,399
That's how you turn people.

707
00:33:39,524 --> 00:33:41,693
I'd expected a denial,
to be honest.

708
00:33:41,985 --> 00:33:43,695
Do we need to continue?

709
00:33:43,820 --> 00:33:48,074
Um, that does tend
to disqualify you, Mr. Jane.

710
00:33:48,241 --> 00:33:50,660
So, um, if you have
nothing further...

711
00:33:50,785 --> 00:33:52,787
She's already given me
valuable information.

712
00:33:52,912 --> 00:33:55,874
- Let's not stop me now.
- Valuable information like what?

713
00:33:57,167 --> 00:33:58,835
With all due respect,
this is not the time

714
00:33:59,002 --> 00:34:00,962
or the place to share the details.

715
00:34:01,129 --> 00:34:03,256
If you wanna see
Lorelei Martins again

716
00:34:03,381 --> 00:34:05,967
this is both the time
and the place.

717
00:34:06,968 --> 00:34:09,471
She told me that
all Red John's friends...

718
00:34:11,139 --> 00:34:14,476
have a secret sign they use
to identify each other.

719
00:34:15,477 --> 00:34:16,936
And what is it?

720
00:34:17,604 --> 00:34:18,938
Go on.

721
00:34:19,689 --> 00:34:22,692
They carry a glass bead
in their pocket...

722
00:34:23,026 --> 00:34:25,445
blood red,
the size of a pea.

723
00:34:26,237 --> 00:34:30,116
- Lorelei showed me hers.
- That's it? Un-provable trivia?

724
00:34:30,283 --> 00:34:32,786
- It proves she trusts me.
- It proves nothing.

725
00:34:32,911 --> 00:34:34,871
Can we stop this farce now?

726
00:34:35,121 --> 00:34:38,249
It is a bit thin, Mr. Jane.
Is that all you have?

727
00:34:38,375 --> 00:34:39,542
No.

728
00:34:40,877 --> 00:34:42,879
- Not at all.
- Well?

729
00:34:43,046 --> 00:34:44,881
Red John has an accomplice...

730
00:34:45,507 --> 00:34:47,717
- inside the FBI.
- Come on.

731
00:34:47,842 --> 00:34:49,844
Judge, this man is just spinning
fantasies now.

732
00:34:49,969 --> 00:34:52,514
Yes. Yes, you would say that.
I saw you.

733
00:34:53,181 --> 00:34:54,516
What do you mean by that?

734
00:34:54,683 --> 00:34:57,811
When I mentioned the glass bead
you suddenly looked very guilty

735
00:34:57,936 --> 00:34:59,646
and you glanced
at your right-hand jacket pocket.

736
00:34:59,813 --> 00:35:01,439
What's in there, Mancini?

737
00:35:02,399 --> 00:35:04,609
This... this is the same thing
that you did to Norris.

738
00:35:04,776 --> 00:35:05,902
- What? Who?
- Son of a bitch...

739
00:35:06,027 --> 00:35:08,655
- Agent.
- What's in your pocket, Mancini?

740
00:35:08,780 --> 00:35:12,075
There's nothing... this is
a childish trick, Your Honor.

741
00:35:12,200 --> 00:35:15,370
Th-this man has just planted
a bead on me.

742
00:35:15,495 --> 00:35:18,415
Uh, let's be clear.
I have not touched you.

743
00:35:18,540 --> 00:35:20,959
Everybody in this room
has seen that.

744
00:35:21,126 --> 00:35:23,378
But you're saying
that there is in fact

745
00:35:23,503 --> 00:35:25,338
a red glass bead
in your pocket.

746
00:35:25,463 --> 00:35:27,298
- Is that what you're saying?
- No!

747
00:35:27,549 --> 00:35:29,134
You're putting words in my mouth.

748
00:35:29,259 --> 00:35:31,720
Show us what's in your pockets, agent.

749
00:35:31,886 --> 00:35:33,555
- You don't understand...
- Show us!

750
00:35:39,811 --> 00:35:41,062
He planted it.

751
00:35:42,021 --> 00:35:43,523
He planted it!

752
00:35:43,648 --> 00:35:45,900
But he didn't touch you, did he?

753
00:35:48,361 --> 00:35:50,321
You son of a bitch!

754
00:35:50,780 --> 00:35:51,823
- Mancini!
- Come here!

755
00:35:51,990 --> 00:35:54,159
- Order! Order!
- Get over here!

756
00:35:55,368 --> 00:35:58,455
Agent Shultz! This is a disgrace.

757
00:36:02,834 --> 00:36:05,128
- Ah, well done.
- Good job. When do we get her back?

758
00:36:05,295 --> 00:36:07,839
Uh, judge says we can pick her up
at county jail tomorrow.

759
00:36:07,964 --> 00:36:10,467
Did, uh, Mancini really throw
a bottle at you?

760
00:36:10,592 --> 00:36:13,011
Yes, he did, and then he proceeded
to chase me

761
00:36:13,178 --> 00:36:16,514
through the state house,
but failed to catch me.

762
00:36:16,973 --> 00:36:19,434
Congratulations.
Another mortal enemy made.

763
00:36:19,559 --> 00:36:20,894
You should be very proud.

764
00:36:21,019 --> 00:36:22,812
Uh, meanwhile,
we've got a case to solve.

765
00:36:22,937 --> 00:36:24,773
Well, let's get busy then, boss.

766
00:36:25,607 --> 00:36:27,442
So let's just assume that Rex

767
00:36:27,567 --> 00:36:29,694
was at Callie's apartment
to fix her computer.

768
00:36:29,819 --> 00:36:31,112
What happened next?

769
00:36:31,237 --> 00:36:33,031
How does that escalate
to a double murder?

770
00:36:33,156 --> 00:36:34,365
Well, maybe the computer
is key.

771
00:36:34,491 --> 00:36:36,242
Maybe there was something important
on the hard drive.

772
00:36:36,367 --> 00:36:38,495
She cleans hotel rooms.
What could be important?

773
00:36:38,620 --> 00:36:41,206
How does that connect
her lipstick on his cheek?

774
00:36:41,331 --> 00:36:43,792
He couldn't fix her computer
so they made out instead?

775
00:36:43,917 --> 00:36:46,461
Well, there are other reasons
for kissing someone.

776
00:36:47,045 --> 00:36:49,631
Celebration, for instance,
hence the champagne.

777
00:36:49,798 --> 00:36:51,007
What would they be celebrating?

778
00:36:51,132 --> 00:36:53,426
Well, maybe the kiss was
"Thanks for trying to fix my computer."

779
00:36:53,593 --> 00:36:55,929
So who's the third person here?
What are we missing?

780
00:36:56,262 --> 00:36:58,473
Sorry I'm late.
They're setting up a stage

781
00:36:58,598 --> 00:37:01,059
for the state lottery prize
presentation at the capital.

782
00:37:01,184 --> 00:37:03,895
- Traffic on L Street was crazy.
- Oh, the lottery.

783
00:37:04,020 --> 00:37:05,563
They should do that
at Raley Field

784
00:37:05,688 --> 00:37:06,981
or someplace
where they have parking.

785
00:37:07,106 --> 00:37:08,900
Uh, when did computer forensics
say they'd be done

786
00:37:09,025 --> 00:37:10,276
with Callie's hard drive?

787
00:37:10,401 --> 00:37:11,736
End of the week, but...

788
00:37:11,861 --> 00:37:13,488
- What?
- Callie's sister... Nicola.

789
00:37:13,613 --> 00:37:14,906
You have her phone number?

790
00:37:18,660 --> 00:37:21,079
Ladies and gentlemen, friends

791
00:37:21,204 --> 00:37:24,624
it is my very great pleasure
to introduce to you at this time

792
00:37:24,749 --> 00:37:28,378
the lucky winner of this year's
biggest lottery jackpot.

793
00:37:28,586 --> 00:37:30,129
Please welcome to the stage

794
00:37:30,255 --> 00:37:35,260
a young woman
who is now worth $56 million...

795
00:37:35,468 --> 00:37:36,970
Valerie Whittaker.

796
00:37:37,095 --> 00:37:38,680
Come on out here, Valerie.

797
00:37:39,681 --> 00:37:41,558
- There you go, Valerie.
- Wow!

798
00:37:41,724 --> 00:37:43,643
- Congratulations.
- Thank you!

799
00:37:44,227 --> 00:37:46,646
Thank you so, so, so much.

800
00:37:46,813 --> 00:37:49,315
I'm so blessed. Thank you.

801
00:37:49,440 --> 00:37:50,692
Valerie, how you feeling?

802
00:37:50,900 --> 00:37:54,070
Oh... I'm just in shock.
It's like a movie.

803
00:37:54,195 --> 00:37:56,573
- Any plans for the money?
- Not yet.

804
00:37:56,739 --> 00:37:57,782
I'm gonna take a flier.

805
00:37:57,907 --> 00:38:00,785
Do you happen to know a Tom Yannick
of the Sacramento Police?

806
00:38:02,245 --> 00:38:03,830
- No.
- Are you sure?

807
00:38:03,955 --> 00:38:05,498
'Cause I'm pretty sure.

808
00:38:05,623 --> 00:38:09,210
Who else would've had the opportunity?
A random intruder? Unlikely.

809
00:38:09,335 --> 00:38:12,297
Tom Yannick.
He's not your boyfriend then?

810
00:38:12,964 --> 00:38:14,215
Okay. Just a moment.

811
00:38:15,174 --> 00:38:17,260
Valerie, this is Nicola Karlsen.

812
00:38:17,552 --> 00:38:19,679
She's Callie Karlsen's sister

813
00:38:20,054 --> 00:38:22,557
the woman that was brutally murdered
for the lottery ticket

814
00:38:22,682 --> 00:38:24,100
that won that check
you're holding there.

815
00:38:24,225 --> 00:38:26,311
Would you tell her
you don't know Tom Yannick?

816
00:38:27,770 --> 00:38:29,981
- I...
- Aha!

817
00:38:32,942 --> 00:38:35,445
- You told me nothing would go wrong!
- No! Stop, stop!

818
00:38:35,570 --> 00:38:37,864
Thomas Yannick...
you're under arrest for murder.

819
00:38:39,365 --> 00:38:40,617
Yes.

820
00:38:41,034 --> 00:38:42,785
This doesn't belong to you.

821
00:38:44,078 --> 00:38:46,748
We're gonna have to get
the name changed.

822
00:38:46,873 --> 00:38:49,709
Do you have a... marker, pen?

823
00:38:50,376 --> 00:38:52,253
Callie was checking
the lottery numbers

824
00:38:52,378 --> 00:38:54,005
while Rex tried to fix
her computer.

825
00:38:55,006 --> 00:38:57,550
She won $56 million.

826
00:39:00,261 --> 00:39:01,638
"She kissed Rex"

827
00:39:01,804 --> 00:39:03,389
"got the champagne
out of the fridge"

828
00:39:03,681 --> 00:39:05,058
"then she called her sister."

829
00:39:06,225 --> 00:39:08,269
Then greed got
the better of Rex

830
00:39:08,978 --> 00:39:11,689
and he tried to strangle Callie
so he could steal the ticket.

831
00:39:12,815 --> 00:39:14,442
"But she killed him instead
with a champagne bottle"

832
00:39:14,567 --> 00:39:15,944
and called 911.

833
00:39:16,235 --> 00:39:19,447
Then half-strangled
and in shock, she fainted.

834
00:39:20,615 --> 00:39:22,158
And that's where you come in.

835
00:39:22,867 --> 00:39:26,412
"You found the two of them, you saw the
lottery ticket and the champagne bottle."

836
00:39:26,537 --> 00:39:29,165
"You put 2 and 2 together...
quite the detective."

837
00:39:29,332 --> 00:39:30,708
"So you killed Callie."

838
00:39:32,335 --> 00:39:34,879
You think about it for a while,
or you just go for it?

839
00:39:37,256 --> 00:39:39,133
I-I thought about it
for a while.

840
00:39:40,218 --> 00:39:41,970
I felt bad for her.

841
00:39:42,845 --> 00:39:45,640
- But $56 million, man.
- Yeah.

842
00:39:46,975 --> 00:39:48,685
Well, you should've thought
about it a while longer.

843
00:39:52,522 --> 00:39:55,149
Thank you.
Thank you, thank you.

844
00:39:55,942 --> 00:39:57,485
You are such a good man.

845
00:39:59,112 --> 00:40:00,279
Thank you.

846
00:40:02,824 --> 00:40:04,492
Sorry to interrupt, Nicola

847
00:40:04,617 --> 00:40:06,494
but Jane and I have
to pick up a prisoner.

848
00:40:07,662 --> 00:40:08,913
Thank you.

849
00:40:09,080 --> 00:40:10,331
Pleasure.

850
00:40:17,839 --> 00:40:20,883
Come on!
What is taking so long?

851
00:40:21,050 --> 00:40:22,719
Relax. She'll be here.

852
00:40:23,094 --> 00:40:25,596
Look, I-I'm sorry, by the way.

853
00:40:25,722 --> 00:40:28,766
For what? There's a long list
of possibilities.

854
00:40:28,891 --> 00:40:30,643
Yeah, well, this is more of a...

855
00:40:30,768 --> 00:40:33,187
general purpose apology.

856
00:40:33,312 --> 00:40:34,731
Use it for your top issue.

857
00:40:35,732 --> 00:40:36,858
Thanks.

858
00:40:38,985 --> 00:40:41,320
- Here you go.
- Who's this?

859
00:40:41,863 --> 00:40:43,239
5467B.

860
00:40:43,406 --> 00:40:45,616
That's not her.
There's been a mistake.

861
00:40:45,783 --> 00:40:49,078
No mistake.
Her paperwork's all in order.

862
00:40:49,245 --> 00:40:51,080
It's the only
Lorelei Martins we got.

863
00:41:00,590 --> 00:41:03,301
"Stay tuned for scenes
from our next episode."

